<article class="env-remark" id="0CXT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CXT">Remark <span data-tag="0CXT">98.20.2</span> <span class="named">(Strong effectiveness)</span>.</a>  Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a category fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Assume we have </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
an affine open $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\Lambda ) \subset S$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
an inverse system $(R_ n)$ of $\Lambda $-algebras with surjective transition maps whose kernels are locally nilpotent, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
a system $(\xi _ n)$ of objects of $\mathcal{X}$ lying over the system $(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R_ n))$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In this situation, set $R = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits R_ n$. We say that $(\xi _ n)$ is <em>effective</em> if there exists an object $\xi $ of $\mathcal{X}$ over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ whose restriction to $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R_ n)$ gives the system $(\xi _ n)$. </p>
</article>